  "name": "Burger highlife (Ghanaian-German synth highlife)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Highlife made in the 1980s by Ghanaian migrant musicians in West Germany, above all in Hamburg, and carried back to Kumasi and Accra; the name, taken from Hamburg, became the Ghanaian slang borga for migrants returned from abroad. Synthesizers, drum machines and electric bass replaced the horn and guitar-band line-ups while Twi singing and highlife guitar figures stayed; generic synthesizer and drum-machine cards stand in for the varied gear.",
